{"voice":"Leela","pages":[{"text":"Have you ever seen a magnet stick to a refrigerator?","words":[[0,0.28],[0.33,0.42],[0.5,0.76],[0.82,1.07],[1.13,1.15],[1.25,1.71],[1.78,2.09],[2.16,2.25],[2.32,2.35],[2.43,3.67]]},{"text":"Magnets can pull certain metals like iron and steel.","words":[[0,0.57],[0.63,0.79],[0.87,1.14],[1.21,1.64],[1.71,2.14],[2.21,2.46],[2.54,2.9],[2.96,3.08],[3.15,3.99]]},{"text":"The pulling power of a magnet is called magnetic force.","words":[[0,0.19],[0.26,0.66],[0.74,1.11],[1.2,1.29],[1.37,1.39],[1.47,1.9],[1.97,2.08],[2.16,2.47],[2.53,3.06],[3.16,3.95]]},{"text":"Magnetic force is invisible, but we can see what it does.","words":[[0,0.65],[0.73,1.09],[1.14,1.24],[1.32,1.94],[1.96,2.14],[2.19,2.31],[2.37,2.54],[2.61,2.82],[2.87,3.06],[3.12,3.22],[3.29,4.09]]},{"text":"Every magnet has two ends called poles.","words":[[0,0.35],[0.43,0.86],[0.92,1.08],[1.15,1.33],[1.43,1.67],[1.73,2.01],[2.07,2.93]]},{"text":"The two poles are called the North pole and the South pole.","words":[[0,0.2],[0.26,0.46],[0.57,1],[1.06,1.18],[1.23,1.53],[1.56,1.63],[1.71,2.04],[2.11,2.5],[2.55,2.71],[2.76,2.83],[2.9,3.3],[3.37,4.13]]},{"text":"When the North pole meets the South pole, they pull toward each other.","words":[[0,0.27],[0.29,0.36],[0.45,0.8],[0.88,1.21],[1.26,1.54],[1.59,1.66],[1.74,2.13],[2.21,2.72],[2.93,3.13],[3.23,3.52],[3.61,4.05],[4.11,4.33],[4.4,5.11]]},{"text":"But when two North poles meet, they push away from each other.","words":[[0,0.23],[0.29,0.5],[0.57,0.78],[0.87,1.18],[1.25,1.63],[1.71,2.07],[2.28,2.48],[2.57,2.87],[2.93,3.18],[3.24,3.44],[3.51,3.7],[3.76,4.46]]},{"text":"Magnets are used in many things like speakers, doors, and toys.","words":[[0,0.61],[0.67,0.85],[0.93,1.21],[1.25,1.35],[1.43,1.7],[1.76,2.1],[2.16,2.38],[2.44,3.27],[3.41,4.02],[4.06,4.26],[4.35,5.25]]},{"text":"Magnets may be small, but their invisible force is very powerful.","words":[[0,0.57],[0.65,0.82],[0.89,1.01],[1.06,1.71],[1.92,2.11],[2.16,2.37],[2.45,3.15],[3.22,3.6],[3.66,3.77],[3.91,4.23],[4.31,5.39]]}]}